{"id":"curses.ascii/unctrl","module":"curses.ascii","qualname":"unctrl","name":"unctrl","kind":"function","parent":null,"signatures":["unctrl(c)"],"doc":"Return a string representation of the ASCII character c. If c is printable, this string is the character itself. If the character is a control character (0x00–0x1f) the string consists of a caret ('^') followed by the corresponding uppercase letter. If the character is an ASCII delete (0x7f) the string is '^?'. If the character has its meta bit (0x80) set, the meta bit is stripped, the preceding rules applied, and '!' prepended to the result.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/curses.ascii.html#curses.ascii.unctrl","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/curses/ascii.py","line":89},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
